## Type Safety
- No `any` types — use explicit types on all public APIs
- Export types alongside data for consumer convenience
- Discriminated unions for state (e.g., `{ kind: "saved" } | { kind: "failed"; message: string }`)

## Style
- No comments unless the WHY is non-obvious
- No unnecessary abstractions — 3 similar lines > premature DRY
- Minimal diffs — don't refactor adjacent code
- No features beyond what the task requires
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones

## Patterns Used in This Codebase
- Graceful degradation: if Supabase not configured → skip silently, don't throw
- Validation before action: validate submission → then insert (with DB constraint as backup)
- Brief builders: every scoring function has a `buildXxxBrief()` that produces copyable text
- Static content modules: typed exports in `src/data/`, imported by pages at build time
- Tool pattern: `src/lib/<tool>/` (pure logic) + `src/pages/tools/<slug>.astro` (UI)

## Verification
- Run `bun run typecheck` before considering work done
- If you touched src/lib/ or src/data/: also run `bun run coverage`
